You are free to share and adapt this data for any purpose, including
commercially, provided you:

  ATTRIBUTION   — credit dumbindex (https://dumbindex.com) and link the licence.
  SHARE-ALIKE   — license your derivative catalogue under CC BY-SA 4.0 as well.

Why share-alike rather than something more permissive: the value of this data
is that it is checked and kept current, and a catalogue that can be enclosed
stops being checkable. If you build on it, the result should stay as open as
what you started from.

A NOTE ON ACCURACY

This data describes what devices required at the time each record was verified.
Every record carries its `last_verified` date and its sources so you can check
it yourself. Manufacturers change device behaviour after sale — that is the
entire reason this project exists — so a record is a dated observation, not a
guarantee about a device you buy tomorrow. Re-check before relying on it.

Provided as-is, with no warranty. See /how-to-check on the site for the method,
and /corrections for how to tell us we got something wrong.
